('790854c3-25d6-46d7-8173-d0cdb85b11e0', 'life_science', 'year_8', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A trait passed from parent to offspring, such as eye colour, is called:', '["An inherited trait","A learned behaviour","A mutation only","An adaptation only"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Inherited traits are passed genetically from parents to their offspring.', 'AC9S8U02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('a53d1c70-b7d9-41e1-884c-ee93e78a9abc', 'life_science', 'year_8', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'What are microorganisms too small to see without a microscope, such as bacteria, generally called?', '["Cells only","Tissues","Fungi only","Microbes"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Microbes (or microorganisms) are tiny living things, including bacteria and some fungi and viruses.', 'AC9S8U02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('86b39d8e-f376-4bfa-b591-957f45768cc6', 'life_science', 'year_9', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'What is the molecule that carries genetic information in living cells?', '["Glucose","DNA","RNA only","Protein"]'::jsonb, 1, 'DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) carries the genetic instructions used in the growth and functioning of living organisms.', 'AC9S9U03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('77def386-4f12-4f80-a33c-a06bf88d196c', 'life_science', 'year_9', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'The process by which organisms best suited to their environment are more likely to survive and reproduce is called:', '["Natural selection","Photosynthesis","Fermentation","Pollination"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Natural selection is the process where organisms with favourable traits are more likely to survive and pass those traits on.', 'AC9S9U03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('b0f3fe36-1292-48a9-a45c-96d253ac6692', 'life_science', 'year_9', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'In an ecosystem, energy generally flows in which direction through a food chain?', '["From consumers to producers","Equally in both directions","It does not flow, only matter does","From producers to consumers"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Energy flows from producers (which capture energy from sunlight) up through the levels of consumers in a food chain.', 'AC9S9U03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('4080e668-6840-4eb2-a059-eece6007a29b', 'life_science', 'year_10', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'The process by which the body maintains a stable internal environment is called:', '["Respiration","Digestion","Homeostasis","Metabolism"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Homeostasis is the regulation of internal conditions, such as temperature, to keep the body stable.', 'AC9S10U01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('092c450c-1e6d-46fb-ab36-eb483275c87c', 'life_science', 'year_10', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which scientist is most associated with the theory of evolution by natural selection?', '["Charles Darwin","Louis Pasteur","Gregor Mendel","Isaac Newton"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Charles Darwin proposed the theory of evolution by natural selection in his book "On the Origin of Species".', 'AC9S10U01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('da82552d-59a3-4e77-ac3a-5eef92ac4957', 'life_science', 'year_10', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Using living organisms or their processes to develop products, such as genetically modified crops, is called:', '["Astronomy","Meteorology","Geology","Biotechnology"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Biotechnology applies biological processes and organisms to develop products and technologies.', 'AC9S10U01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('27876fbb-4ec2-4cfa-8a50-2c410ab85990', 'life_science', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Which of these describes something that is NOT alive?', '["It grows over time","It needs food and water","It can reproduce","It does not grow, move on its own, or need food"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Living things grow, need food and water, and can reproduce; non-living things do none of these.', 'AC9S3U01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
