('e23c338f-0435-4e3e-83f2-1b8ef76f3fac', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'One word in this sentence is spelt incorrectly. Write the correct spelling of that word.
She could here the birds singing outside.', null, null, 'The correct spelling is "hear".', 'AC9E4LY10', null, null, true, 'hear', null, null, null),
('f8fe27ab-de50-4900-b1f5-e963de22f90b', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'One word in this sentence is spelt incorrectly. Write the correct spelling of that word.
My favourite subject is sience.', null, null, 'The correct spelling is "science".', 'AC9E4LY10', null, null, true, 'science', null, null, null),
('0fb6d6f7-751f-4e9b-b3b1-a7f332c60264', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'One word in this sentence is spelt incorrectly. Write the correct spelling of that word.
They were very exited about the excursion.', null, null, 'The correct spelling is "excited".', 'AC9E4LY10', null, null, true, 'excited', null, null, null),
('26f90851-9201-49b9-a69c-e8a728a5d2a2', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which sentence uses commas correctly?', '["We packed apples, bananas and grapes.","We packed apples bananas and grapes.","We packed, apples bananas and grapes.","We, packed apples bananas, and grapes."]'::jsonb, 0, 'Commas separate items in a list. In Australian English the last two items are joined by "and" without a comma before it.', 'AC9E4LY09', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('566fd545-2a6d-4319-979c-c51134b63d1b', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'Which word is the adverb in this sentence?
The dog barked loudly at the postman.', '["dog","barked","loudly","postman"]'::jsonb, 2, 'An adverb tells us more about a verb. "Loudly" describes how the dog barked.', 'AC9E4LY09', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('328c347c-0685-4924-89a4-5337fe268aec', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Choose the correct word.
The cat washed ____ paws.', '["it''s","its’","it is","its"]'::jsonb, 3, '"Its" shows possession. "It’s" is short for "it is", which would not make sense here.', 'AC9E4LY09', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('d0b7eaee-51f8-43c6-bd2c-4cf0c7ccfe44', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'Which sentence is written in the past tense?', '["We walk to the shops.","We walked to the shops.","We are walking to the shops.","We will walk to the shops."]'::jsonb, 1, 'The past tense describes something that has already happened. "Walked" is the past tense of "walk".', 'AC9E4LY09', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('8028253d-7298-42b6-8a01-fcb28c216ec0', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Where should the apostrophe go?
That is my sisters bike.', '["sisters’","sister’s’","sister’s","no apostrophe is needed"]'::jsonb, 2, 'One sister owns the bike, so the apostrophe goes before the s: "my sister’s bike".', 'AC9E4LY09', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('88c493cf-ac45-48cf-81ce-b2ce3233fe52', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'Which sentence uses a question mark correctly?', '["What time does the bus leave?","What time does the bus leave.","What time does the bus leave!","What time, does the bus leave"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A sentence that asks something ends with a question mark.', 'AC9E4LY09', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('a6483088-2428-4842-ab39-1ae9c512dbe3', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_4', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which word is a conjunction in this sentence?
I wanted to swim, but the pool was closed.', '["but","wanted","swim","closed"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A conjunction joins two parts of a sentence. "But" joins "I wanted to swim" and "the pool was closed".', 'AC9E4LY09', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('51ce6ddf-e0cd-4406-a8df-99582a1ee6ef', 'grammar_punctuation', 'grade_6', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'One word in this sentence is spelt incorrectly. Write the correct spelling of that word.
