Each pack has s stickers.
Which equation matches this story?', '["4s + 3 = 43","4 + 3s = 43","4s − 3 = 43","3s + 4 = 43"]'::jsonb, 0, '4 packs of s stickers is 4s stickers, and the 3 free stickers are added on, making 43: 4s + 3 = 43. So each pack has 10 stickers.', 'AC9M6A02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('93a39e73-15e8-4cba-b609-0bb968499e95', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_6', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'What are the coordinates of point Q?', '["(1, −4)","(−4, 1)","(4, −1)","(−4, −1)"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Q is 4 units to the left of the y-axis and 1 unit up, so its coordinates are (−4, 1). The x-coordinate always comes first, which is why (1, −4) is wrong.', 'AC9M6SP02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('fae48cc1-7c21-4073-a351-7f2dd459235e', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'The bottom line is a straight line.
