('f68c77c5-a936-492c-bb20-d36d790bb3e5', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Three angles meet at a point.
What is the size of angle b?', '["90°","110°","210°","120°"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Angles at a point add to 360°. One angle is a right angle, 90°, so b = 360 − 90 − 150 = 120°.', 'AC9M6M04', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('8abb1006-e865-48bc-8847-37f58fe905e9', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_6', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'What is the size of the angle shown on the protractor?', '["40°","50°","130°","140°"]'::jsonb, 0, 'One arm is along 0° on the outer scale, so read the outer scale where the other arm crosses it: 40°. Reading the inner scale gives 140°.', 'AC9M6M04', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('854948c1-be53-472d-b8b1-6ec430cf4464', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'What is the area of the shaded shape?', null, null, 'Split it into two rectangles: the top one is 5 × 2 = 10 cm² and the bottom one is 3 × 2 = 6 cm². 10 + 6 = 16 cm².', 'AC9M6M02', null, null, true, '16 cm²', ARRAY['16']::text[], null, null),
('bc722676-aa80-466a-a569-5d95bc1f0124', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'A rectangular room has the measurements shown.
What is the area of the floor?', '["10.5 m²","21 m²","52 m²","26 m²"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Area of a rectangle = length × width = 6.5 × 4 = 26 m². The answer 21 m² is the perimeter, and 10.5 just adds the two lengths.', 'AC9M6M02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('1df408c8-d6e5-4f98-a729-61c7cc81bd78', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'The model is built from cubes with no gaps.
