What is the range?', null, null, 'The range is the largest value take away the smallest: 6 − 0 = 6.', 'AC9M6ST01', null, null, true, '6', null, null, null),
('33d97c21-691b-4c61-bf92-48a9600e828f', 'statistics_probability', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'The graph shows how many boys and girls play each sport.
Which sport has more girls than boys?', '["Soccer","Tennis","Netball","Swimming"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Only for netball is the girls’ bar taller than the boys’ bar: 12 girls and 3 boys. For the other sports, more boys play.', 'AC9M6ST01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('217b3847-77dd-44a9-a54e-6d8e8a15f6c7', 'statistics_probability', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'A bag has 3 red, 5 blue and 2 green counters.
A counter is picked without looking.
What is the probability that it is blue?', '["1/5","1/3","5/8","1/2"]'::jsonb, 3, 'There are 3 + 5 + 2 = 10 counters and 5 are blue, so the probability is 5/10, which is 1/2. The answer 5/8 leaves out the green counters.', 'AC9M6P01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('e7f21bf5-39c1-44b3-94ed-83a0e2d0a4ff', 'statistics_probability', 'grade_6', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Pat spins this spinner 40 times.
About how many times would you expect it to land on yellow?', '["4","20","10","40"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Yellow is 1 of 4 equal parts, so it should come up about a quarter of the time. A quarter of 40 is 10.', 'AC9M6P02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('1198ac2a-c76f-46ef-bc14-9469ce7166ff', 'statistics_probability', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'The stem-and-leaf plot shows the ages of the people at a party.
How many people at the party were older than 30?', '["3","4","8","5"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The people older than 30 are 31, 33 and 36 (the 3 stem) and 42 and 45 (the 4 stem). That is 5 people.', 'AC9M6ST01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('ebc84121-ae84-4bdf-962b-e55f3e926c71', 'statistics_probability', 'grade_6', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'Which of these is a statistical question?', '["How tall is the school flagpole?","What is 25 × 4?","What time does school start?","How many hours of sleep do Year 6 students usually get?"]'::jsonb, 3, 'A statistical question is answered by collecting data that varies. Students get different amounts of sleep, so answering it needs data from many students. The others have one fixed answer.', 'AC9M6ST02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('4e8ac5e6-1787-4fa7-98fd-f25015024566', 'statistics_probability', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'The pictograph shows where students would most like to go on holiday.
How many students chose the beach?', null, null, 'Each circle stands for 10 students, so half a circle stands for 5. The beach has 4 whole circles and a half: 40 + 5 = 45.', 'AC9M6ST01', null, null, true, '45', ARRAY['45 students']::text[], null, null),
('55c1ea6d-5a8c-414e-a24c-9b5cc5ab318a', 'statistics_probability', 'grade_6', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'The chance of rain tomorrow is 70%.
What is the chance that it will not rain tomorrow?', '["0.3","0.7","7%","130%"]'::jsonb, 0, 'It either rains or it does not, so the two chances add to 100%. 100% − 70% = 30%, which is 0.3 as a decimal.', 'AC9M6P01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('d5746b12-d745-49f4-9eeb-e41c79352a51', 'statistics_probability', 'grade_6', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Ruby tossed a coin 50 times.
The table shows her results.
Which statement is true?', '["There were 8 more heads than tails.","Heads came up more than half of the time.","The coin must be unfair.","Tails came up 28 times."]'::jsonb, 1, 'Half of 50 is 25, and heads came up 28 times, which is more than half. There were 6 more heads, not 8. A fair coin often gives results like this, so we cannot say it is unfair.', 'AC9M6P02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('aa19e7d2-e581-46ff-91d0-455fae993076', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'Mia used these blocks to make a number.
What number did she make?', '["352","325","532","3052"]'::jsonb, 0, 'There are 3 hundreds, 5 tens and 2 ones, which make 352. 325 swaps the tens and the ones.', 'AC9M3N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('a5863566-1a42-4a5d-9875-6c8820183bf8', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Which number is six hundred and forty?', '["46","604","640","6040"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Six hundred is 600 and forty is 40, so the number is 640. 604 has 4 ones instead of 4 tens.', 'AC9M3N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('08faba14-b0b5-420f-9452-2e4fe70a45cf', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Which number is the arrow pointing to?', '["31","35","36","40"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The marks go up by 5: 30, then 35. The arrow is on the mark halfway between 30 and 40, so it shows 35.', 'AC9M3N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('bc256ecb-533b-4cf4-baac-166308e46f29', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which list shows the numbers in order from smallest to largest?', '["159, 95, 519, 915","915, 519, 159, 95","95, 519, 159, 915","95, 159, 519, 915"]'::jsonb, 3, '95 is the only number without hundreds, so it is smallest. Then compare the hundreds: 159 has 1 hundred, 519 has 5 and 915 has 9.', 'AC9M3N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('8424c496-de8b-407b-97f7-00425f475153', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'Ella has these coins in her purse.
How much money does she have?', null, null, 'The dollar coins make $2 + $1 = $3. The other coins make 50c + 20c + 20c + 10c = $1. Altogether that is $4.', 'AC9M3N07', null, null, true, '$4', ARRAY['4', '4.00', '$4.00', '4 dollars']::text[], null, null),
('3e50f13b-2e47-4f52-a7bb-5b08717ce5cf', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Sam wants to buy a drink that costs 85c.
Which group of coins makes exactly 85c?', '["","","",""]'::jsonb, 2, 'Group C is 50c + 20c + 10c + 5c = 85c. Group A makes 90c, group B makes 80c and group D makes $1.', 'AC9M3N07', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('852d52f6-3454-4530-95e3-bb13507305b1', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'Lily buys the ball and the book.
How much does she spend?', null, null, 'The ball costs $6 and the book costs $4, and $6 + $4 = $10.', 'AC9M3N07', null, null, true, '$10', ARRAY['10', '10.00', '$10.00', '10 dollars']::text[], null, null),
('402c248f-7e22-4829-a405-e62cc5ef48ca', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Noah buys the cap.
