How much change should he get?', '["$5","$8","$12","$28"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The change is $20 − $8 = $12. $5 is the change for the shirt, and $28 adds the money instead of taking it away.', 'AC9M3N07', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('628d3485-fe90-449c-a8a4-40ce8aa3f2ae', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'Ms Ray puts star stickers on the class chart in rows.
How many stickers are there?', null, null, 'There are 4 rows with 5 stickers in each row, and 4 × 5 = 20.', 'AC9M3N06', null, null, true, '20 stickers', ARRAY['20']::text[], null, null),
('26444ab9-c0bc-44ce-af24-59cc3ee367d4', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'The dots show the muffins in a baking tray.
Which number sentence matches the tray?', '["3 + 6","3 × 6","6 − 3","3 × 3"]'::jsonb, 1, 'There are 3 rows of 6 muffins, which is 3 groups of 6: 3 × 6. Adding 3 + 6 counts only one row and one column.', 'AC9M3N06', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('174d47dc-544a-4613-8b5f-3797fcea8679', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'Mrs Kim has 24 pencils.
