How many pencils go on each table?', null, null, '24 shared into 4 equal groups is 6 in each group, because 4 × 6 = 24.', 'AC9M3N06', null, null, true, '6 pencils', ARRAY['6']::text[], null, null),
('fe4a6008-556f-4833-932f-aa6ccde5fbe2', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', '45 students go on an excursion in two buses.
28 students are on the first bus.
How many students are on the second bus?', '["17","23","27","73"]'::jsonb, 0, '45 − 28 = 17. One way: 28 + 2 = 30, then 30 + 15 = 45, and 2 + 15 = 17. 73 adds the numbers instead, and 23 takes the smaller digit from the larger one in each place.', 'AC9M3N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('3c5a4827-e8f2-4aa4-bc91-a9422b81f51f', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'What fraction of the circle is shaded?', '["1/3","1/4","3/4","4/1"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The circle has 4 equal parts and 1 is shaded, so 1/4 is shaded. 3/4 is the part that is not shaded.', 'AC9M3N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('f8d5aa2a-7a3b-404f-80c3-56d0093fdac7', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'A block of chocolate has 10 equal pieces.
The shaded pieces have been eaten.
What fraction of the block has been eaten?', '["3/10","3/7","7/10","10/3"]'::jsonb, 0, '3 of the 10 equal pieces are shaded, so 3/10 has been eaten. 3/7 compares the eaten pieces with the pieces that are left.', 'AC9M3N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('f81eefc0-e7cb-456f-b71f-b9ad1319e9ee', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which shape has one third shaded?', '["","","",""]'::jsonb, 2, 'One third means 1 of 3 equal parts, which is shape C. Shape A has two thirds shaded, B has one quarter and D has one sixth.', 'AC9M3N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('8f5d702f-52f1-4145-b582-db464578f060', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which story matches the number sentence 12 − 5?', '["Sam had 12 stickers and gave 5 away.","Sam had 12 stickers and got 5 more.","Sam put 12 stickers in each of 5 rows.","Sam shared 12 stickers between 5 friends."]'::jsonb, 0, 'Taking away 5 from 12 matches giving 5 stickers away. Getting 5 more is 12 + 5, and 12 stickers in each of 5 rows is 5 × 12.', 'AC9M3A01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('f1b0e374-8d4d-4561-ab01-b56ee4e9c1b9', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'The school farm collected 146 eggs on Monday and 128 eggs on Tuesday.
How many eggs did the farm collect altogether?', null, null, 'Add the hundreds, tens and ones: 100 + 100 = 200, 40 + 20 = 60 and 6 + 8 = 14. Then 200 + 60 + 14 = 274.', 'AC9M3N03', null, null, true, '274 eggs', ARRAY['274']::text[], null, null),
('eafc1eef-3537-4fc9-ac76-88f50ea14b28', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'There were 63 people on a train.
At the station, 27 people got off.
How many people are still on the train?', '["36","44","46","90"]'::jsonb, 0, '63 − 27 = 36. One way: 63 − 20 = 43, then 43 − 7 = 36. 90 adds the numbers, and 44 takes 3 from 7 instead of regrouping.', 'AC9M3N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('7af71d83-61d8-4634-b06c-9fef08315fff', 'number_operations', 'grade_3', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'Tickets to the school play cost $5 each.
