Which statement is true?', '["He is unlikely to take out a red ball.","He will probably take out a blue ball.","He cannot take out a red ball.","He is certain to take out a red ball."]'::jsonb, 3, 'Every ball in the bag is red, so the ball he takes out must be red. That is certain. There are no blue balls, so a blue ball is impossible.', 'AC9M3P01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('222f9ed1-2b59-422d-8085-cf5807851ec6', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Which number is shown by the arrow?', '["2.03","2.3","2.13","3.2"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The line from 2 to 3 is split into tenths. The arrow is 3 tenths past 2, which is 2.3. 2.03 would be 3 hundredths past 2.', 'AC9M5N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('e21913a5-a4de-4123-bd3d-e8156a828b84', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Four friends ran a 100 m race.
The table shows their times.
Who won the race?', '["Aria","Ben","Cody","Dina"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The winner has the shortest time. All the times start with 14, and 14.08 has 0 tenths, fewer than any other, so Cody won. Ben’s 14.6 is the slowest time, not the fastest.', 'AC9M5N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('14876250-a1b9-4a7d-95ee-2295ca9f953f', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'In which number does the digit 7 have a value of 7 tenths?', '["2.57","7.25","72.5","2.75"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The tenths are the first place after the decimal point. In 2.75 the 7 is in that place. In 2.57 the 7 is 7 hundredths.', 'AC9M5N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('bc0ff119-fdaf-4619-9608-3c5c02e4a38c', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which number is a factor of 36 and also a factor of 48?', '["8","9","12","18"]'::jsonb, 2, '36 ÷ 12 = 3 and 48 ÷ 12 = 4, so 12 is a factor of both. 8 does not divide 36, and 9 and 18 do not divide 48.', 'AC9M5N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('c1797886-ee4c-4e00-a52c-68ff6f1e60d1', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Mr Tran has 84 chairs.
He puts them in rows with the same number in each row and none left over.
Which of these could be the number of chairs in each row?', '["5","8","9","12"]'::jsonb, 3, '84 ÷ 12 = 7, so 7 rows of 12 use every chair. 84 cannot be shared into equal rows of 5, 8 or 9 without some left over.', 'AC9M5N02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('c8569993-3ec9-49b6-8fec-2b5285fbbc6a', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which mixed number is the arrow pointing to?', '["1 1/4","1 3/4","1 3/8","7/8"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Each whole is split into 4 equal parts, so each mark is one quarter. The arrow is 3 quarters past 1, which is 1 3/4.', 'AC9M5N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('c4a47546-d2fe-4076-bd1c-ccb6ac432421', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Which strip has more than one half shaded?', '["","","",""]'::jsonb, 2, 'Strip C has 5 of 8 equal parts shaded, and 5/8 is more than 4/8, which is one half. Strip B is exactly one half, and strips A and D are less than half.', 'AC9M5N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('b4832762-18af-4573-8936-0010b4a3d5fb', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'short_answer', 'Pia ate 2/8 of a pizza.
Her brother ate 3/8 of the same pizza.
What fraction of the pizza did they eat altogether?', null, null, 'Both fractions are eighths, so add the eighths: 2 eighths + 3 eighths = 5 eighths, which is 5/8. Adding the bottom numbers as well would wrongly give 5/16.', 'AC9M5N05', null, null, true, '5/8', null, null, null),
('cec6df0a-9eeb-495e-8320-ea551d4d8207', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'What percentage of the grid is shaded?', '["35%","65%","3.5%","0.35%"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The grid has 100 equal squares and 35 are shaded. 35 out of 100 is 35%. 65% is the part that is not shaded.', 'AC9M5N04', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('c313cc16-2659-45f4-99f4-7ac0486c6ebc', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Which fraction is the same as 25%?', '["1/25","1/4","2/5","25/10"]'::jsonb, 1, '25% means 25 out of 100, and 25/100 simplifies to 1/4. 1/25 would be only 4%.', 'AC9M5N04', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('ee0c2a37-171b-4b92-888e-1bfdad44eb9e', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'A school buys 24 boxes of pencils.
