('eb7bb278-ed6f-4f1d-999b-b0aec64ea8cf', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', '86 students are going on camp.
Each tent holds 4 students.
What is the smallest number of tents needed?', '["20","21","22","24"]'::jsonb, 2, '86 ÷ 4 = 21 remainder 2. 21 tents hold 84 students, and the 2 students left over need one more tent, so 22 tents are needed.', 'AC9M5N07', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('811b3ca1-51d0-4136-89ca-0720771652ef', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Which is the best estimate of 398 × 5?', '["200","1000","1500","2000"]'::jsonb, 3, '398 is close to 400, and 400 × 5 = 2000. So 398 × 5 is a little less than 2000.', 'AC9M5N08', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('79caa324-ae64-4efa-86f7-436682d7f0c6', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'Leo paid for these items with a $20 note.
