('a6b577a4-3564-4bf3-9aee-95872e3b34a2', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which of these masses is the heaviest?', '["3.5 kg","3.45 kg","3.05 kg","3.405 kg"]'::jsonb, 0, 'All four start with 3 kg, so compare the tenths: 3.5 has 5 tenths and the others have 4 or 0. 3.405 has the most digits but is not the heaviest.', 'AC9M5N01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('559168f3-cf52-45b1-be18-799ed7c7ce0b', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Each circle is one whole.
What number is shown by the shaded parts?', '["2 1/2","2 1/4","3 1/2","10/12"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Each circle is split into quarters and 10 quarters are shaded: two whole circles and 2 quarters of the third. 2 2/4 is the same as 2 1/2. 10/12 treats all three circles as one whole.', 'AC9M5N03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('aab4839f-e392-4420-882e-56e7e97c4a56', 'number_operations', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Buses that seat 30 students will take 240 students on an excursion.
