('08506427-3239-4d8d-ace4-22c38d17d076', 'number_patterns', 'grade_5', 'advanced', 'short_answer', 'Nina makes square frames from tiles.
How many tiles will she need for Design 6?', null, null, 'The designs use 8, 12 and 16 tiles, so each design needs 4 more tiles than the one before. Design 4 needs 20, Design 5 needs 24 and Design 6 needs 28.', 'AC9M5A01', null, null, true, '28 tiles', ARRAY['28']::text[], null, null),
('93f6666b-be39-4541-bc44-26b17ca932bb', 'number_patterns', 'grade_5', 'advanced', 'short_answer', 'Jai puts numbers into a number machine.
The table shows what comes out.
What number comes out when 10 goes in?', null, null, 'Each output is 3 times the input, plus 2: 3 × 3 + 2 = 11 and 5 × 3 + 2 = 17. So 10 gives 10 × 3 + 2 = 32.', 'AC9M5A03', null, null, true, '32', null, null, null),
('9048017b-73c5-4fbe-9539-d873ae8d3ecd', 'number_patterns', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'What is the value of 5 × (8 − 3)?', '["13","25","37","40"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Work out the brackets first: 8 − 3 = 5. Then 5 × 5 = 25. Ignoring the brackets and working left to right gives 5 × 8 − 3 = 37.', 'AC9M5A02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('4efe55a0-e6e2-40b8-a742-cdfc65bea091', 'number_patterns', 'grade_5', 'advanced', 'multiple_choice', 'The scales are balanced.
The two blocks marked ? g have the same mass.
What is the mass of one of those blocks?', '["6 g","11 g","12 g","22 g"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The left side must also be 17 g. Take away the 5 g block: 17 − 5 = 12 g for the two blocks together, so each is 12 ÷ 2 = 6 g. 12 g is both blocks, not one.', 'AC9M5A02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('2f858cb3-39ce-4ae9-9974-2ada33e63b23', 'number_patterns', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'The rule for a pattern is “start at 4 and add 7 each time”.
Which number is in the pattern?', '["24","28","32","35"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The pattern goes 4, 11, 18, 25, 32, … so 32 is in it. 28 and 35 are multiples of 7, but the pattern starts at 4, not 0.', 'AC9M5A01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('267ebb5f-5a35-4caa-8e66-d2c3ce11a91f', 'number_patterns', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'What number goes in the box to make this number sentence true?
□ × 8 = 72 − 16', null, null, '72 − 16 = 56, so □ × 8 = 56. Since 7 × 8 = 56, the missing number is 7.', 'AC9M5A02', null, null, true, '7', null, null, null),
('8802e3c5-490b-4e79-af50-88bacd53795d', 'number_patterns', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Mei counts on by the same amount each time.
0.4, 0.8, 1.2, 1.6, …
What is the 8th number she says?', '["2.8","3.0","3.2","3.6"]'::jsonb, 2, 'She adds 0.4 each time, so the 8th number is 8 × 0.4 = 3.2. 2.8 is the 7th number.', 'AC9M5A01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('b22fd128-5810-4619-ad8d-1faae27ff7e9', 'number_patterns', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'Which number sentence is true?', '["36 ÷ 4 = 4 ÷ 36","6 × 7 = 7 × 6","20 − 5 = 5 − 20","12 ÷ 2 = 12 × 2"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Multiplying in either order gives the same answer: 6 × 7 and 7 × 6 both make 42. Swapping the numbers in a subtraction or a division changes the answer.', 'AC9M5A01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('9b616fb0-992e-4420-8618-f8e2c93a2fe7', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'The clock shows when a train leaves, in 24-hour time.
What is this time in 12-hour time?', '["3:40 am","5:40 am","5:40 pm","3:40 pm"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Times after 12:00 in 24-hour time are in the afternoon or evening. 15 − 12 = 3, so 15:40 is 3:40 pm. 5:40 comes from taking away 10 instead of 12.', 'AC9M5M03', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('f3729a60-cbd5-4210-bbe5-2c34d77bb5da', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'short_answer', 'Ella catches Bus B at the library.
How long does it take her to get to the station?', null, null, 'Bus B leaves the library at 8:47 and reaches the station at 9:14. From 8:47 to 9:00 is 13 minutes, and from 9:00 to 9:14 is 14 more: 13 + 14 = 27 minutes.', 'AC9M5M03', null, null, true, '27 minutes', ARRAY['27', '27 min', '27 mins']::text[], null, null),
('ac6a2d3a-b337-4370-8ffa-be6478095c5e', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'What is the area of this shape?', '["12 cm²","14 cm²","16 cm²","24 cm²"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Count the squares: 4 + 4 + 2 + 2 = 12, and each is 1 cm², so the area is 12 cm². 16 is the perimeter in centimetres, not the area.', 'AC9M5M02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('162655aa-0632-43f5-8556-1ee29c402c3b', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'advanced', 'short_answer', 'The diagram shows the shape of a garden bed.
What is the perimeter of the garden bed?', null, null, 'The two unlabelled sides are 12 − 5 = 7 m and 9 − 4 = 5 m. The perimeter is 12 + 4 + 7 + 5 + 5 + 9 = 42 m. Adding only the four labelled sides gives 30 m.', 'AC9M5M02', null, null, true, '42 m', ARRAY['42']::text[], null, null),
('49baedba-68a6-46aa-8fe7-1447decc7de4', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'What is the size of the angle shown on the protractor?', '["60°","65°","115°","125°"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Start from the 0 on the arm lying along the base line and read that scale: the other arm is at 65°. 115° comes from reading the other scale.', 'AC9M5M04', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('7275f3c9-a638-465d-9da0-1ff44ae30ddf', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which angle is obtuse?', '["","","",""]'::jsonb, 2, 'An obtuse angle is bigger than a right angle but smaller than a straight line, like angle C. A is a right angle, and B and D are acute.', 'AC9M5M04', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('69fabf0f-3596-48bb-b10c-9c269cdccacd', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Which of these nets will NOT fold to make a cube?', '["","","",""]'::jsonb, 3, 'Net D is a 2 by 3 block. When it is folded, two squares land on top of each other and one face of the cube is left open. Nets A, B and C each fold into a cube.', 'AC9M5SP01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('7ae65bb3-b1af-4674-a31a-9579f72152bb', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'developing', 'multiple_choice', 'How many faces does this triangular prism have?', '["3","5","6","9"]'::jsonb, 1, 'A triangular prism has 2 triangle faces at the ends and 3 rectangle faces around the sides: 2 + 3 = 5. 9 is the number of edges.', 'AC9M5SP01', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('5cd80e1b-eff1-4e5c-8bc7-6d825d00fda0', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'foundation', 'multiple_choice', 'The map shows a campsite.
In which square is the well?', '["B2","E2","2E","E3"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Go across to column E, then up to row 2: the well is in E2. The column letter is written first.', 'AC9M5SP02', null, null, true, null, null, null, null),
('27df8834-714f-410b-8770-df86bdc73671', 'geometry_measurement', 'grade_5', 'proficient', 'multiple_choice', 'Sam walks from home to school along the path shown.
